AB  - Agricultural researchers face challenges in publishing and sharing data-driven crop yield models, limiting transparency and collaboration. Additionally, collecting and preprocessing data from diverse sources is often inefficient. We present GreenHub, a first step toward a platform that streamlines both data access and model deployment for crop yield forecasting. GreenHub provides (i) public access to standardized, high-quality datasets; (ii) a uniform interface and Python-based library for flexible data retrieval; and (iii) hosting of machine learning models. Data sources include weather forecasts, soil properties, and vegetation indices. Researchers can upload models with minimal integration effort, and the platform automatically executes and visualizes model predictions for public access. This enables model comparison and fosters collaboration while saving researcher’s time. By lowering technical barriers, GreenHub offers an efficient ecosystem that lays the groundwork for developing, deploying, and sharing crop yield prediction models.
