AB  - The passing of Ilya M. Sobol’ marks the loss of an influential mathematician whose work pioneered and fundamentally shaped global sensitivity analysis (GSA) and modern uncertainty quantification. This tribute reflects on Sobol's foundational role in GSA, with particular emphasis on the variance-based framework, now widely known as the Sobol’ method. Drawing on historical context and personal recollections from two of his long-time colleagues, it honors Sobol's scientific and human legacy while considering the continuing importance of sensitivity analysis for understanding increasingly complex and integrated models under uncertainty.
